(CURVE METRICS ULTIMATE INTERVIEW GUIDE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(HOW TO USE THIS GUIDE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This guide is designed to help you explain the project at multiple levels:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(? short answers for fast interview responses) Tj
T*
(? medium-depth answers for follow-up rounds) Tj
T*
(? deep architectural answers for senior and system design interviews) Tj
T*
(? project-specific questions tied to what is actually in the codebase) Tj
T*
(? interviewer-style questions based only on what you say out loud) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Best practice in interviews:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Start high-level.) Tj
T*
(2. Explain responsibilities before implementation details.) Tj
T*
(3. Say why a design exists, not just what it does.) Tj
T*
(4. Mention one tradeoff and one future improvement.) Tj
T*
(5. Be honest about weaknesses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(30-SECOND PROJECT SUMMARY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This project is a CMS-driven full stack platform with three main parts: an admin app for ) Tj
T*
(content authoring and publishing, a shared contract layer for layout/block normalization and) Tj
T*
( validation, and a public Next.js website that server-renders published content. The most ) Tj
T*
(important architectural decision is a revision-based page workflow, so drafts, preview, ) Tj
T*
(restore, and publishing are all first-class instead of directly editing live content.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1-MINUTE PROJECT SUMMARY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The platform is split into `admin`, `shared`, and `curvemetricswebsite`. The admin app is ) Tj
T*
(where internal users manage pages, media, templates, and publishing workflows. The shared ) Tj
T*
(layer defines canonical schemas, block contracts, normalization logic, and runtime ) Tj
T*
(validation so preview and production interpret content the same way. The public website is ) Tj
T*
(intentionally thin: it fetches a validated page bundle from the admin content API, derives a) Tj
T*
( render view, and server-renders the final page. The strongest part of the design is the ) Tj
T*
(revision-first page lifecycle. The biggest weakness is that public delivery still depends on) Tj
T*
( the admin/content runtime at request time, which creates scalability and availability ) Tj
T*
(concerns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2-MINUTE ARCHITECTURE ANSWER) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I would explain the system as a CMS-style platform built around content lifecycle safety. ) Tj
T*
(The admin app owns writes and workflows like edit, autosave, preview, restore, and publish. ) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
