(Instead of storing only the current page state, the system stores revisions, so draft ) Tj
T*
(content and published content are separate. The shared layer owns the canonical meaning of ) Tj
T*
(blocks and layouts. It handles normalization, validation, and bundle assembly. The public ) Tj
T*
(site does not interpret raw CMS data directly. It fetches a validated page render bundle and) Tj
T*
( renders it through SSR. That separation is intentional because it reduces preview-versus-) Tj
T*
(production drift. The main tradeoff is increased application-level complexity, but the ) Tj
T*
(benefit is much stronger control over content correctness and publishing safety.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PROJECT SCOPE AND BUSINESS PURPOSE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
