(pointer updates. The public content API builds a canonical render bundle rather than ) Tj
T*
(returning raw DB records. This gives the frontend a stable rendering contract while keeping ) Tj
T*
(content meaning centralized. The strongest part of the backend is the revision-first page ) Tj
T*
(pipeline. The biggest architectural weakness is that public delivery still depends on the ) Tj
T*
(authoring runtime at request time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TOUGH INTERVIEW QUESTIONS WITH STRONG DIRECTION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHY IS RUNTIME DEPENDENCY BETWEEN PUBLIC SITE AND ADMIN DANGEROUS?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Because public traffic becomes dependent on the same backend that serves authoring ) Tj
T*
(workflows. That creates availability coupling, scaling tension, and operational risk. If ) Tj
T*
(public traffic spikes, it can affect content editors. If admin/content assembly slows down, ) Tj
T*
(it directly impacts public latency. A stronger design would separate published-content ) Tj
T*
(delivery into a read-optimized path or precomputed artifact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHY DIDN?T YOU JUST USE WORDPRESS OR A NORMAL CMS?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Because the main challenge wasn?t just content fields, it was lifecycle control and render ) Tj
T*
(contract consistency. I wanted revision-based draft/preview/publish flow and a shared ) Tj
T*
(interpretation layer that keeps preview and production aligned.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(IF TRAFFIC BECAME 100X LARGER, WHAT WOULD YOU CHANGE FIRST?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I would first decouple public content delivery from the admin runtime. That gives the ) Tj
T*
(biggest immediate improvement to scalability and public reliability. After that, I?d add ) Tj
T*
(shared caching, read-optimized published bundles, and stronger observability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHAT WOULD YOU IMPROVE FIRST FOR PRODUCTION SECURITY?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I would replace the current admin-only auth model with real users, hashed credentials or ) Tj
T*
(SSO, stronger role-based authorization, and audit logging. I would also harden uploads and ) Tj
T*
(content sanitization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHAT WOULD YOU IMPROVE FIRST FOR FRONTEND MAINTAINABILITY?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I would split the editor shell into smaller state-owning modules and improve lazy loading ) Tj
T*
(for heavy editor features.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(TECHNOLOGY CHOICE Q&A) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHY REACT?) Tj
